# fib_iterative — iterative Fibonacci with a real loop (README §13). Two mutable
# accumulators advance through fib via repeated addition; `+ 0` calls copy values
# (mutable rebind via call output), and a counter drives the loop. The result
# comes from the loop, not a constant.
#
# Correctness observation: fib(10) = 55 (fib(0)=0, fib(1)=1).
# Expected output: 55

FibIterative is project
FibIterative module examplesFibIterative
FibIterative target console
FibIterative entry main

examplesFibIterative is module
examplesFibIterative path examples.fibIterative
examplesFibIterative exports main
examplesFibIterative purpose "Compute the 10th Fibonacci number iteratively"
examplesFibIterative invariant "Loop runs until the counter reaches the targetIndex index"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Iteratively compute and print fib(10)"
main invariant "Writes exactly one integer line: 55"
main let prev mutable Int64 0
main let cur mutable Int64 1
main let count mutable Int64 1
main let zero immutable Int64 0
main let targetIndex immutable Int64 10
main let oneStep immutable Int64 1
main let harnessName immutable String "fib_iterative"
main let harnessExpected immutable Int64 55
main let noopDecoy immutable Int64 0
main let noopName immutable String "fib_iterative: real result (not the no-op 0)"
main at loopHead do checkDone
main branch ifFalse stillGoing goto loopExit
main do nextFib
main do copyPrev
main do copyCur
main do bump
main goto loopHead
main at loopExit do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

checkDone is call
checkDone in main
checkDone invokes math.lessThanInt64
checkDone arg left Int64 count
checkDone arg right Int64 targetIndex
checkDone out stillGoing Bool

nextFib is call
nextFib in main
nextFib invokes math.addInt64
nextFib arg left Int64 prev
nextFib arg right Int64 cur
nextFib out nextValue Int64

copyPrev is call
copyPrev in main
copyPrev invokes math.addInt64
copyPrev arg left Int64 cur
copyPrev arg right Int64 zero
copyPrev out prev Int64

copyCur is call
copyCur in main
copyCur invokes math.addInt64
copyCur arg left Int64 nextValue
copyCur arg right Int64 zero
copyCur out cur Int64

bump is call
bump in main
bump invokes math.addInt64
bump arg left Int64 count
bump arg right Int64 oneStep
bump out count Int64

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 cur


noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 noopDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 cur

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode